      "writtenOn": "2014-12-05T03:10:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i don\u0027t understand why this is being added or what you are testing it on. technically, we shouldn\u0027t be receiving source cap packets in this state because the source should be dropping VBUS and then re-applying it. and on our platforms, as soon as VBUS is re-applied, we transition out of this state in to the discovery state.\n\nhowever, some products can\u0027t detect VBUS (such as hoho and dingdong boards). on these boards todd is adding a CONFIG_ option to say we can\u0027t detect VBUS, and in this case, I agree this code should be added.\n\nsee https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/#/c/233270/1 for related changes.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 837,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 837,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "c060fc79404c1a37acdb7665229fec02dd65261e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ffa51f3_fb7bcf5e",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 837,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120324
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-12-05T04:08:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Instead of 233270, I noticed 233024: \"pd: dingdong/hoho: Fix hard reset recovery timeout.\", is the one by Todd that is a fix for this state, as mentioned by you.\n\nTodd\u0027s fix should do: we will have different waiting interval so as to _catch_ the moment when SRC-CAP is re-sent, by SINK side\u0027s returning to SNK_DISCONNECTED state again.\n\nRegarding the testing platform, unfortunately BizLink is just at an early stage with mixture of our boards \u0026 STM32 Discovery EVA boards and jump-wires: that\u0027s why we are easier to fall trapped into this SNK_HARD_RESET_RECOVER state :-)\n\nAlso, BizLink\u0027s main Type-C products are on peripheral side -- more on SNK role: simpler as hoho/dingdong (boards just done PCBA and is finding ways to verify), but more complex as docking (boards next week, adopting partially \u0026 mixing from hoho \u0026 samus_pd)\n\nFor now, I can only hope if this code is accepted, since ours is not a real environment, and not sure how will it impact the real one.",
      "parentUuid": "1ffa51f3_dbe413f4",
      "revId": "c060fc79404c1a37acdb7665229fec02dd65261e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1ffa51f3_bbd5c7fc",
        "filename": "common/usb_pd_protocol.c",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 1242,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-12-05T03:10:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "this change is dangerous. unfortunately the state of the code is such that adding length to printf\u0027s can cause timing issues with PD communication.\n\ni suggest adding this debug code to debug_level 1:\nif (debug_level \u003e\u003d 2)\n\tpd_dump_packet(port, msg);\nelse if (debug_level \u003e\u003d 1)\n\tCPRINTF(\"RX ERR (%s %d)\\n\", msg, bit);\nelse\n\tCPRINTF(\"RX ERR (%d)\\n\", bit);\n\nand then you can use debug level 1 to get the information you want, but it won\u0027t be printed by default.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1242,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 1242,
        "endChar": 21
      },
      "revId": "c060fc79404c1a37acdb7665229fec02dd65261e",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
